  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_2' aria-label=\" Habban Shah versus Sheruddin pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('2','2026','2026_5_404_420','2026INSC451'); ><font size='4'> <strong>HABBAN SHAH<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>SHERUDDIN </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 5 S.C.R. 404</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 451</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001512026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : PANKAJ MITHAL<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SARASA VENKATANARAYANA BHATTI</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue arose whether the decree of specific performance passed by the court of first instance directing for the execution of sale deed on deposit of the balance sale consideration within three months would be inexecutable for the reason that the balance sale consideration Act,1963 &ndash; s.28 &ndash; Code of Civil Procedure, 1908 &ndash; Ord. XX r.12A &ndash; Specific performance &ndash; Executability of conditional decree &ndash; Non-deposit of balance sale consideration within stipulated time &ndash; Defendant-appellant entered into agreement to sell the<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 06-05-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 7062/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('2','2026','2026_5_404_420','2026INSC451','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-out